    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdd controlled C21/C22 Harness enhancement validation and a manual four-target hosted candidate. The suite distinguishes a lost native write receipt from a lost final broker receipt, checks exact targets across two logical nodes and two terminal operators, and prevents automatic rename replay after read-only recovery.\n\n```text\nmanual enhancement qualification (rc.5 / Node 22.23.4)\n  verified official npm archives → isolated runtime\n  11 native checks → fresh run/source/target report validation\n  confirmed normal release → owned installation cleanup\n  unknown release → retain evidence and task root\n```\n\nThe workflow targets Windows x64, Linux x64, macOS Intel and ARM. Existing communication/onboarding workflows and production src/integrations remain unchanged. Short fixture-only socket directories and explicit POSIX process-group release evidence prepare the platform candidate.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** No standalone enhancement CI runner/report contract; the original nested POSIX socket layout exceeds the shared 103-byte budget, and a POSIX host exit code alone can accept forced cleanup.\n  **After:** RED/GREEN checkpoints and 33 focused tests cover fresh reports, process/result mismatch, retained unknown release, socket isolation and normal POSIX cleanup.\n- Fixed Node22.23.4 `npm run check`: **2906 passed / 11 existing skipped**, 246 files passed / 3 skipped; lint, imports and build passed.\n- Formal Windows rc.5 npm/Web verification: **11 checks passed**, including both lost receipts, membership protection and real ConPTY confirmation/target retention. The new runner boundary accepted a fresh run and confirmed resource release.\n- Native wrapper verification reused the retained official rc.5 dependencies; it does not claim a new installer lifecycle, hosted runs, Linux/macOS native acceptance, formal Desktop or physical cross-machine validation.\n- [Candidate and boundaries](docs/development/dsh-enhancement-hosted-candidate-20261106.md) · [Evidence index](docs/development/evidence/c22-dsh-hosted-candidate-20261106/validation.json)\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** validation\n\nThe new workflow has only workflow_dispatch and read permissions, with no schedule, retry loop or Issue writes. GitHub requires the new manual workflow on the default branch before dispatch. This draft covers candidate review and ordinary CI; merge and native four-target execution remain separate decisions.\n",
